A||||4||JohnnyK||Very hot engine compartment: Normal?||||1||
Z||000000||JohnnyK||07-30-2000||07:24 PM||||After driving my Fiero for a while, the back end of the car gets real hot, and the black vents on the back almost too hot (especially the one over the battery) The temp guage isn't going up (It goes to, approx, between the quarter and half notch.) My question is, how can this battery made out of plastic take this heat? Won't it melt??||||reg||1
Z||000001||Sillhouette.com||07-30-2000||07:35 PM||||Look at your exhaust manifolds throught the grille.  If they are red that means that your timing is out. Get it retimed otherwise it is normal.  Don't forget that air flows throught from the bottom of the car up through those wents.  That is why the vents are hot and the battery is kind of to the side of it.  Anyways the batteries are built quite durable with all sorts of safety built in them to dispense acid in the event of an overheat.  <P>Later||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||07-30-2000||07:41 PM||||Yeah its normal. You can cook hamburgers on my vents after a few minutes of driving...they're designed that way.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||squid||07-30-2000||08:33 PM||||You didnt say if you had a 4 or a 6 cylinder. The exhaust manifold on the 4's eventually crack all the way around. My #1 cylinder tube had a 1/4" gap all the way around and made the back glass almost too hot to touch. A new manifold is @$105 from The Fiero Store.  ||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||07-30-2000||11:51 PM||||Well,,,,, I fooled with this awhile back. I stuck a 300F max digital cooking thermometer between the grate and the deck lid.<P>On a 70F day the engine compartment temp was over 150F driving at lower speeds. In stop and go it can climb over 200F real easy.<P>Yes, allong with other things I'm working on I'm looking at ways to cool it down. So far I think adding the aftermarket scoops on the sides are the best bet. Use one for engine intake and the other just to move air into the engine bay. Anything that stirs up the air in there will help.||||reg||1
